  "query_preview": "..\n\nTonight into tomorrow night: A low pressure system associated \nwith a cold front is currently advancing through the region. On \nand off rain showers will slowly progress southeastward before \ncoming to an end after 5 PM today across the north. Lingering \nshowers are expected across the south tonight. A wetting rain (one\ntenth of an inch of rain or more) is most likely to occur in \nPhillips and western Valley county from now through noon today.\n\nA shortwave ridge is expected to move in on Saturday night before\nthe next moderate strength trough moves in. On Sunday through\nMonday night, rainfall totals are expected to range from around 5\nhundredths up to 8 tenths of an inch. The higher end of this range\nexists over Phillips county and areas close to the Canadian\nborder. A Lake Wind Advisory will be considered for breezy\nconditions on Sunday and Monday for Fort Peck Lake. Nelson\nReservoir and Medicine Lake are not part of these advisories, but\nwill still see challenging boating conditions.\n\nTuesday Moving Forward: A weak ridging pattern is expected to be\nin place with a brief chance of showers on Wednesday. There is\nuncertainty on rain amounts, but there is less than 5 hundredths\nat any given location as of the latest forecast.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nIncreased PoPs and winds through this evening.\n\nThere is moderate confidence in rain amounts through Tuesday.\n\nThere is moderate to high confidence of wind gusts reaching 30 to\n40 mph on Sunday and Monday on Fort Peck Lake.",
